cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its result records, please cite the paper
  "JUBILEE: A Benchmark Environment for Off-Policy Evaluation in Debt
  Collections" and this software.
type: software
title: "JUBILEE: benchmark environment and reproduction materials for off-policy evaluation in debt collections"
authors:
  - given-names: Diego Silva
    family-names: Prado
    affiliation: Alpha Synthesis Labs
  - given-names: Tiago Amaral Penteado
    name-particle: de
    family-names: Jesus
    affiliation: Alpha Synthesis Labs
  - given-names: Bruno Caldas
    name-particle: de
    family-names: Souza
    affiliation: Alpha Synthesis Labs
  - given-names: Cristiano Bevitori Maffia
    name-particle: De
    family-names: Oliveira
    affiliation: Alpha Synthesis Labs
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alpha-synthesis/jubilee"
abstract: >-
  Simulator of a relational loan-month collections world with known generating
  process, hidden confounders and a randomized exploration share, an
  off-policy-evaluation estimator panel, and the protocols, result records and
  scripts that rebuild the tables of the JUBILEE paper. Simulator model 2.1.0
  (full settlement) and a snapshot of model 2.0.0.
keywords:
  - off-policy evaluation
  - benchmark
  - debt collections
  - causal inference
  - hidden confounding
  - simulation
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24008544"
    description: "Data deposit: cohort extracts and result records"
